Anchor page popups below the shell's browser controls.

The shell's top bar is browser controls: the page is moved down by
translating the view's window (ApplyTopControlsOffset in
aura_shell_runtime_bridge.cc). A window's bounds leave out its own
transform, so WebContentsViewAura::GetContainerBounds() -- which autofill and
password suggestions add a field's position to -- reported the page a whole
top bar higher than it was drawn, and the popup opened over the address bar.
On OHOS the container's origin now includes that translation; its size is
left alone.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-popup-below-browser-controls.patch

diff --git a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc
index 8525b80..a55881f 100644
--- a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc
+++ b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_view_aura.cc
@@ -25,6 +25,9 @@
 #include "base/task/current_thread.h"
 #include "base/task/thread_pool.h"
 #include "build/build_config.h"
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+#include "base/numerics/safe_conversions.h"
+#endif
 #include "components/input/render_widget_host_input_event_router.h"
 #include "components/viz/common/features.h"
 #include "content/browser/browser_plugin/browser_plugin_guest.h"
@@ -931,7 +934,26 @@ gfx::NativeWindow WebContentsViewAura::GetTopLevelNativeWindow() const {
 }
 
 gfx::Rect WebContentsViewAura::GetContainerBounds() const {
-  return GetNativeView()->GetBoundsInScreen();
+  gfx::Rect bounds = GetNativeView()->GetBoundsInScreen();
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+  // The shell's browser controls move the page down by translating the
+  // view's window (ApplyTopControlsOffset in aura_shell_runtime_bridge.cc).
+  // A window's bounds leave out its own transform, so popups that add an
+  // element's position to these bounds -- autofill and saved passwords under
+  // a field -- opened a whole top bar too high, over the address bar.
+  // Input is unaffected: event targeting goes through the transform.
+  //
+  // Only the origin moves. The size stays the window's, for whatever sizes
+  // itself to the container.
+  if (RenderWidgetHostView* view = web_contents_->GetRenderWidgetHostView()) {
+    if (aura::Window* page = view->GetNativeView();
+        page && page->parent() == GetNativeView()) {
+      bounds.Offset(
+          0, base::ClampRound(page->transform().To2dTranslation().y()));
+    }
+  }
+#endif
+  return bounds;
 }
 
